WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.450
Monday morning.

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.310
Eight PCs in a small office, all online.

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.650
Then a small box under
one desk blinks off,

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.850
and every screen says: No network.

5
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.190
Across town, another office
is wired differently.

6
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.610
One of its links snaps,
and everyone keeps working.

7
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.970
So how can one small box
take a whole office offline?

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.310
In this mission, you'll learn that a
topology is the layout of how the devices

9
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.110
on a network are connected.

10
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:34.130
You'll meet the star, where every device
has its own cable to one central device,

11
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.510
usually a switch.

12
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.570
And the mesh, where devices
connect directly to several others,

13
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.910
so there are many paths between them.

14
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.640
Your mission: work out how one box
can take a whole office offline.
